<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees April CPI at -0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees April CPI at -0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its April consumer price index stood at -0.1 percent month-on-month and +1.5 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In March, the Venice inflation rate rose 0.2 and 2.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		  -0.1   (0.2)	1.5   (2.0)</p>
<p>    Food			     -0.5   (0.0)     -1.2  (-0.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.0   (0.6)	3.0   (3.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 0.5   (0.2)	3.7   (4.3)</p>
<p>    Furniture			-0.1   (0.0)	1.7   (1.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.0  (-0.6)	1.8   (1.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		 -0.1   (0.4)	2.2   (2.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.1  (-0.3)     -2.5  (-2.3)</p>
<p>    Education			-0.1   (0.0)	4.7   (5.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.1   (0.6)	5.4   (6.1)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services    -0.1   (0.2)	0.5   (0.6)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
